From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:17:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 51/61] blitz-dom, blitz-paint: draw a text field's placeholder

An empty input or textarea showed nothing for its `placeholder`. It now
shows the attribute's text in the field's `::placeholder` style, which
gives its font, colour and opacity, where the value would be: centred
in a single-line input's content box, at the top of a textarea and
wrapped to its width. An input's placeholder has its line breaks
removed, as HTML says.

The style is stylo's lazy pseudo-element style, so it is computed when
the field is built and whenever stylo restyles it (`RecalcStyle` lists
the restyled fields), after style resolution, along with the
placeholder's own text layout (`flush_placeholder`). A change of the
attribute restyles the field and so lays the placeholder out again.
Scale changes and a textarea's width reach it as they reach the editor.

blitz-paint draws it while the editor's text is empty. Opacity is
multiplied into the glyphs' colour, since not every renderer applies
the glyph alpha that `draw_glyphs` takes.

`:placeholder-shown` still never matches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
